(a) No alcoholic beverage license shall be granted for, and no person knowingly and intentionally may sell or offer to sell:
(1) Any distilled spirits or fortified wines in or within 100 yards of any church or day care facility licensed as such by the State of Georgia or within 200 yards of any school building, educational building, school grounds, college campus, or public recreation facility;
(2) Any wine or malt beverages within 100 yards of any day care facility licensed as such by the State of Georgia, any church, school building, school grounds, or college campus. Nothing in this subparagraph shall prohibit a grocery store licensed for the retail sale of only wine and malt beverages for off-premises consumption from selling wine or malt beverages within 100 yards of any college campus, where so permitted by resolution or ordinance of the county or municipality. As used in this subparagraph, the term "grocery store" means a retail establishment which has at least 85 percent of its total retail floor space reserved for the sale of food and other nonalcoholic items, conducts all of its alcoholic beverage sales inside the building containing its retail floor space, and meets such other criteria as may be required by the local governing authority of the county or municipality; or
(3) Any proposed location which is within 100 feet of any residentially zoned property; provided that this restriction shall not apply to:
a. Those places of business licensed to sell alcoholic beverages prior to the zoning or rezoning of property as residential which is within the prohibited distance;
b. Those locations which propose to sell alcoholic beverages for on-premises consumption provided that:
1. The proposed location is a distance of at least 50 feet from the nearest residential structure as measured from the nearest comer of the building enclosing the proposed licensed business and the nearest wall of the nearest residential structure being used for housing purposes;
2. The proposed location contains at least 2,000 square feet of enclosed space;
3. The proposed location's primary business is the provision of goods and/or services with the sale of alcoholic beverages being incidental to such use;
4. The proposed location conducts and keeps all sales, consumption, and possession of alcoholic beverages inside the enclosed location;
5. The proposed location reserves at least 75 percent of its retail floor space for the sale of other goods and/or services;
6. The proposed location generates at least 60 percent of its revenue from sources other than the sale of alcoholic beverages; and
7. Where the proposed location directly abuts residentially zoned property there shall be erected and maintained an ornamental masonry wall or other completely opaque wall or barrier at least six feet in height above grade.
(4) Any distilled spirits, fortified wine, wine, or malt beverages within 100 yards of any housing authority, alcoholic treatment center owned and operated by this state or any county or municipal government therein.
(b) Each application for an alcoholic beverage license shall include a certificate of a registered surveyor, indicating therein that such location complies with this section.
(c) The location restrictions herein contained shall not apply to:
(1) Any location for which a license was issued prior passage hereof, nor to the renewal of such license, so long as said license has remained in effect.
(2) Any location for which a new license is applied for if the sale of the alcoholic beverage(s) for which application is made was lawful at such location and such location was in actual operation 180 days immediately preceding such application.
(d) The location restrictions herein contained shall not apply to any location within the special district designated in Charter section 24.1 previously referred to as the Central Business District.
